    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1024">

                <pb facs="0888" n="772" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg772"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/299.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-02T12:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 2, 1912—12 noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 25, 4 p.m. The Government has agreed to take entire Chargé of shipment
                    of American arms from Vera Cruz, furnishing a Federal guard therefor. Minister
                    of Hacienda thinks the usual duty should be paid. Under the circumstances it
                    perhaps ought to be waived, but I think it good policy to accede and pay the
                    duty.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
